 ## Overview
-Voxel-based representations replace the continuous coordinate-based Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) query of standard Neural Radiance Fields with discrete 3D grids storing volumetric features, density, or color [S1]. This family solves the computational bottleneck of repeated MLP evaluations during rendering by enabling hardware-accelerated lookups, caching, or convolutional processing [S1]. It differs from its siblings, such as [NeRF](1185-nerf-neural-radiance-fields.md) which uses dense coordinate queries, by trading spatial continuity for memory efficiency and inference speed, often at the cost of resolution limits imposed by grid size [S1].
+Voxel-based representations use discrete 3D grids to store volumetric features, density, or color [S1]. This approach trades spatial continuity for memory efficiency and inference speed, with resolution limits imposed by grid size [S1].
 
